
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Branded Course Portal</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #f9f9f9;
            color: #333;
        }
        h1 {
            color: #2c3e50;
        }
        .iframe-container {
            width: 100%;
            height: 600px; /* Sets the height of the "window" */
            border: 2px solid #3498db;
            border-radius: 8px;
            overflow: hidden;
            background-color: #fff;
        }
        iframe {
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            border: none; /* Removes the default ugly iframe border */
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- This is YOUR content -->
    <h1>Welcome to Our Learning Portal</h1>
    <p>Below, we are displaying our partner's course catalog. Notice how the URL in your browser's address bar stays exactly the same as this page, even though the content below is loaded from somewhere else.</p>

    <!-- This is the IFRAME (The "Masking" part) -->
    <div class="iframe-container">
        <iframe 
            src="https://in.norton.com/" 
            title="Partner Course Catalog"
            loading="lazy">
            Your browser does not support iframes. Please update your browser.
        </iframe>
    </div>

    <p><em>Educational Note: Try scrolling inside the blue box. You are browsing the external site, but your browser thinks you are still on this page.</em></p>

</body>
</html>
